Qoder CLI compatibility resources

The files in this directory were extracted without modification (native binaries
are stored with lossless gzip compression) from @qoder-ai/qodercli version 1.1.83,
published by Qoder AI. The upstream package distributes them with the Apache
License, Version 2.0, reproduced in LICENSE-APACHE-2.0.

Package URL, npm integrity and the SHA-256 of each file are in manifest.json.
The WASM module's wasm-bindgen ABI is hosted by separately written Rust code;
its cryptographic operations and protocol format are not reimplemented.

The native bridge is Qoder's machine identity (UMID) component. It collects the
machine identity and can contact the SDK's service, as in the official CLI. Its
initialization is separate from the gateway's HTTP transport and is not covered
by the per-account inference proxy. No real credentials or machine identities
are included in the test fixtures. Tests do not execute these native binaries.

Only the binary for the build target is embedded in the gateway executable.
Windows x64 also embeds the companion sgsdk.dll. The official package does not
provide a Windows ARM64 bridge. The explicit legacy setting supports rollback
without executing a native identity bridge.
